# T22650 — S2166.1.10–12 — modbus — read System information — tb470 IE520 stack — 2026-09-29 — FAIL (one register disagrees with the CLI)

Verdict: FAIL on step 5 (Number of Alarms), PASS on the other nine steps. The DUT implements
Mapping Version 5, whose system-block layout differs from the addresses printed in the case
text (which are the version-1 layout); every item the case asks for was located at its
version-5 address and equals the CLI — except the per-member alarm count: register 0x0049
reads 124 while `show alarm facility settings` lists 93 per-member alarms (31 × 3 members).
124 = 31 × 4, i.e. one member's worth too many, matching the stack's PROVISIONED-but-absent
member 2 (`show stack`: "2 - - - - Provisioned"). Whether the register should count a
provisioned slot is a product question — reported as a mismatch, for Terrence.
Run labelled: clean.

Operator: bench-runner subagent (device-testing-61 = sentinel; Terrence away). Queue row 8,
case 5 of 6. Hand-driven: ckcon.py on /dev/u5 + mb.py (pymodbus 3.8.6) from tb470 eth1 →
stack vlan1 10.38.215.10. Full stdout 22650.out, client log mb-22650.log, driver reads3.sh.

